        "scope": "in_scope",
        "statement": "For every set $U$ and every nonzero commutative unitary ring $R$,\n$S_U$ is a commutative periodic monoid and\n\\begin{equation}\n d(S_U,R)=1,\\qquad \\HH=\\Delta_{S_U},\\qquad\n D_{(A,k)}(S_U)=|A|+k\\quad(0\\leq k\\leq2).\n\\end{equation}\nThe positive cyclic semigroup of $(A,k)$ is not a group exactly when\n$k=1$. Every Sch\\\"utzenberger group of $S_U$ is trivial.\nConsequently $S_{\\mathbb N}$ refutes Conjecture~3.26.",
        "status": "needs_attention",
        "target_digest": null,
        "target_path": null,
        "title": "Counterexamples to Wang's Conjectures 3.26 and 5.3 on semigroup algebras",
